faq:
  - q: Can we create our own roles?
    a: Yes. Create roles, choose permissions module by module, set report access and work queue items, and duplicate a role to make a variant. A user can hold more than one role.
  - q: Can a salesperson be limited to their own enquiries?
    a: Yes. Data scopes let a role see only the records assigned to the user, while a manager's role can include records managed by their team.
  - q: Can we hide margins from the sales team?
    a: Yes. Internal costing and margin are shown only to roles that hold the internal costing permission.
  - q: Is there an audit log?
    a: Yes. Administrators can search an audit log, and a user and role activity report shows who did what across the company.
  - q: Can a person approve their own expense?
    a: The person who raised a claim cannot verify it, and submit, verify, approve and post are separate permissions.
